From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda-forge gtk3-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] meson: check sincos with the math.h prototype

Without a prefix, cc.has_function() accepts a compiler builtin. clang >= 22
knows sincos as a builtin, so the check reports it on macOS, whose math.h
does not declare it, and tests/gtkgears.c then fails with "call to
undeclared library function 'sincos'". Check against <math.h> as GTK 4
does since
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/commit/9f64202a60e587871cfcd60a150ca814b1d75970
("meson: Consolidate function checks", GNOME/gtk#5070).
---
 meson.build | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 50d33ba..74e4180 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -250,7 +250,6 @@ check_functions = [
   'rint',
   'log2',
   'exp2',
-  'sincos',
   'trunc',
   'localtime_r',
   'fmin',
@@ -262,6 +261,13 @@ foreach func : check_functions
   endif
 endforeach
 
+if cc.has_function('sincos',
+                   args: '-D_GNU_SOURCE',
+                   prefix: '#include <math.h>',
+                   dependencies: libm)
+  cdata.set('HAVE_SINCOS', 1)
+endif
+
 cdata.set('HAVE_DECL_ISINF', cc.has_header_symbol('math.h', 'isinf') ? 1 : false)
 cdata.set('HAVE_DECL_ISNAN', cc.has_header_symbol('math.h', 'isnan') ? 1 : false)
 
